'''Marikina's 2nd congressional district''' is one of the two [[congressional districts of the Philippines]] in the city of [[Marikina]]. The district covers the seven northern Marikina [[barangay]]s of Concepcion Uno, Concepcion Dos, Fortune, [[Marikina Heights]], Parang, Nangka, and Tumana. 

The district has been represented in the [[House of Representatives of the Philippines]] since 2007.<ref name="congleg">{{cite web|url=http://www.congress.gov.ph/legislators/?v=province |title=Roster of Philippine legislators |publisher=[[House of Representatives of the Philippines]] |accessdate=February 10, 2021}}</ref> An amendment to the 1996 Marikina City Charter, passed in 2006, created the district from [[Marikina's at-large congressional district]].<ref name="apportion">{{cite web|url=https://www.officialgazette.gov.ph/2006/12/15/republic-act-no-9364/ |title=Republic Act No. 9364 |date=December 15, 2006 |publisher=[[Official Gazette (Philippines)]] |accessdate=February 10, 2021}}</ref> 

[[Miro Quimbo]] of the [[Partido Federal ng Pilipinas]], elected as a member of [[Lakas–CMD|Lakas]], has represented the district since 2025.

